From 941b7768f2ca9a58f6cc667af3eff06e98d19d23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karel Zak <kzak@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:39:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/32] lib/fileutils: add safe FD/openat2 helpers

Backport of the lib/fileutils infrastructure the libmount TOCTOU and
SUID hardening depends on.  No functional change on its own; nothing in
this branch calls the new helpers yet.

 * ul_openat_resolve() -- openat2(2) wrapper, returns ENOSYS when the
   syscall is not available.  configure.ac learns to probe for
   <linux/openat2.h>; RESOLVE_NO_SYMLINKS and RESOLVE_BENEATH get a
   fallback definition in include/fileutils.h for build environments
   with older kernel headers.

 * ul_open_no_symlinks() -- opens a path rejecting symlinks at any
   component, not just the last one.  Uses openat2(RESOLVE_NO_SYMLINKS)
   (Linux >= 5.6) and falls back to open(O_PATH) plus a readlink() of
   /proc/self/fd/<fd> when openat2() is unavailable, so that e.g. a
   container seccomp profile answering openat2() with ENOSYS does not
   silently disable the protection.

 * ul_fd_mkpath() -- composes "/proc/self/fd/<fd>" on one place, with
   one buffer size (UL_FDPATH_BUFSIZ).  The pathname was open-coded on
   several places, each with its own size calculation.

 * ul_fd_get_path() -- asks the kernel for the name of an already open
   file.  Refuses names which are not usable for open(): the
   "<path> (deleted)" names of unlinked files, the pseudo-names of
   pipes and sockets, and truncated readlink() results.  This is used
   to canonicalize the pinned mount target, so a silently shortened
   name would end up in the mount table and in utab.

   ul_reopen() is converted to it and thereby gains the same checks.

Backport notes:

 * The patches are taken from the upstream stable/v2.42 branch; each of
   the commits referenced below records the corresponding master commit
   in its own message.  Five commits are squashed into one; fde56542c
   and 67fd3bf43 are fixups of the two commits before them.
 * The monitor_fanotify.c hunk of 14cfec982 is dropped -- the libmount
   monitor is not split into monitor_{fanotify,mountinfo,utab}.c in
   this branch.
 * The refactoring of ul_restricted_path_oper() is not backported; this
   branch still has the fork+drop_permissions code inline in
   lib/canonicalize.c.  Only the ul_fd_get_path() half of that hunk is
   taken.
 * ul_absolute_path(), ul_is_relative_path() and ul_endswith() are
   still called absolute_path(), is_relative_path() and endswith() here.
 * lib/fileutils.c now uses lib/canonicalize.c and lib/strutils.c, so
   test_fileutils has to link libcommon.la.  Upstream did this in the
   unrelated cleanup 1aff73db2; only the single line is taken.

